<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- 2026-09-08: previously the manifest referenced the raw, unstyled
         android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar directly, with none of
         its attributes overridden — meaning the brief pre-Compose window
         (during cold start, before setContent's first frame renders) used
         the platform's default white/gray, unrelated to this app's green
         branding. Kept the same platform theme as parent rather than
         adding a Material Components / AppCompat dependency just for a
         DayNight base — lower risk given this can't be compile-tested
         here — but overrode the attribute that actually controls what's
         visible before Compose takes over. See REQUIREMENTS.md ยง13 and
         ui/theme/Theme.kt for the corresponding Compose-side fix.

         2026-09-20: removed statusBarColor/navigationBarColor — Play
         Console's pre-launch report flags these as deprecated
         edge-to-edge APIs for any app targeting API 35+, regardless of
         whether enableEdgeToEdge() (called in MainActivity.onCreate)
         makes them functionally inert at runtime. System bar appearance
         is now controlled entirely by enableEdgeToEdge()'s explicit
         SystemBarStyle, kept in sync with the resolved app theme
         (including manual dark/light/AMOLED overrides) via a SideEffect
         in ExpenseTrackerTheme — see Theme.kt. -->
    <style name="Theme.ExpenseTracker" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/brand_background_light</item>
    </style>
</resources>